<li data-start=3D"5061" data-end=3D"5148">
<p data-start=3D"5063" data-end=3D"5148">Make a <strong data-start=3D"5070"=
 data-end=3D"5082">new venv</strong> for your competition work (so old ezkl=
 versions don=E2=80=99t haunt you).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5150" data-end=3D"5180">Goal: we get to a point where:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5182" data-end=3D"5302">
<li data-start=3D"5182" data-end=3D"5233">
<p data-start=3D"5184" data-end=3D"5233"><code data-start=3D"5184" data-end=
=3D"5209">python -m neurons.miner</code> (or docker image) runs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5234" data-end=3D"5302">
<p data-start=3D"5236" data-end=3D"5302">Baseline miner returns valid proof=
s with the <strong data-start=3D"5281" data-end=3D"5301">default circuits</=
strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5304" data-end=3D"5307">
<h3 data-start=3D"5309" data-end=3D"5354">Step 1 =E2=80=93 Competition circ=
uit &amp; model spec</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5356" data-end=3D"5439">We treat the <strong data-start=3D=
"5369" data-end=3D"5392">competition_circuit</strong> folder in the repo as=
 the canonical interface:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5441" data-end=3D"5728">
<li data-start=3D"5441" data-end=3D"5486">
<p data-start=3D"5443" data-end=3D"5486">Input shape: <strong data-start=3D=
"5456" data-end=3D"5474">(1, 3, 64, 64)</strong> for image</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5487" data-end=3D"5580">
<p data-start=3D"5489" data-end=3D"5580">Output: <strong data-start=3D"5497=
" data-end=3D"5507">vector</strong>, size determined by competition (for th=
e age one, it=E2=80=99s 21 dims, 0=E2=80=9320).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5581" data-end=3D"5728">
<p data-start=3D"5583" data-end=3D"5728">One of the circuit inputs must be =
a <strong data-start=3D"5619" data-end=3D"5638">float32 <code data-start=3D=
"5629" data-end=3D"5636">nonce</code></strong>, as required in <code data-s=
tart=3D"5655" data-end=3D"5687">custom_circuit_integrations.md</code>. <spa=
n class=3D"" data-state=3D"closed"><span class=3D"ms-1 inline-flex max-w-fu=
ll items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data=
-testid=3D"webpage-citation-pill"><a href=3D"https://github.com/inference-l=
abs-inc/omron-subnet/blob/main/docs/custom_circuit_integrations.md?utm_sour=
ce=3Dchatgpt.com" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener" alt=3D"https://github.=
com/inference-labs-inc/omron-subnet/blob/main/docs/custom_circuit_integrati=
ons.md?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com" class=3D"flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounde=
d-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out=
 text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class=
=3D"relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class=
=3D"flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between overflow-hidden" style=3D"=
opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class=3D"max-w-[15ch] grow truncate ove=
rflow-hidden text-center">GitHub</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5730" data-end=3D"5742">Design rule:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"5744" data-end=3D"5908">
<p data-start=3D"5746" data-end=3D"5908">Whatever architecture we train, we=
 <strong data-start=3D"5781" data-end=3D"5859">must export ONNX that matche=
s the competition circuit=E2=80=99s expected signature</strong> (same input=
s, same output shape, same op types).</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"5910" data-end=3D"5927">We=E2=80=99ll eventually:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5929" data-end=3D"6139">
<li data-start=3D"5929" data-end=3D"5965">
<p data-start=3D"5931" data-end=3D"5965">Implement <code data-start=3D"5941=
" data-end=3D"5953">TinyAgeNet</code> in PyTorch.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5966" data-end=3D"6059">
<p data-start=3D"5968" data-end=3D"5988">Export to ONNX with:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5991" data-end=3D"6059">
<li data-start=3D"5991" data-end=3D"6011">
<p data-start=3D"5993" data-end=3D"6011">opset_version=3D18</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6014" data-end=3D"6059">
<p data-start=3D"6016" data-end=3D"6059">inputs: <code data-start=3D"6024" =
data-end=3D"6031">image</code> (1,3,64,64), <code data-start=3D"6045" data-=
end=3D"6052">nonce</code> (1,)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6060" data-end=3D"6139">
<p data-start=3D"6062" data-end=3D"6139">Plug that ONNX into the competitio=
n circuit pipeline (instead of DummyModel).</p>
</li>
</ul>
