<p data-start=3D"10016" data-end=3D"10033">different hotkeys</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10036" data-end=3D"10090">
<p data-start=3D"10038" data-end=3D"10090">same circuit &amp; model files (=
read-only shared volume)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10091" data-end=3D"10189">
<p data-start=3D"10093" data-end=3D"10109">Watch CPU &amp; RAM:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"10112" data-end=3D"10189">
<li data-start=3D"10112" data-end=3D"10189">
<p data-start=3D"10114" data-end=3D"10189">zk proving is CPU-heavy; sweet s=
pot is usually some fraction of core count.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10190" data-end=3D"10330">
<p data-start=3D"10192" data-end=3D"10197">Tune:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"10200" data-end=3D"10330">
<li data-start=3D"10200" data-end=3D"10264">
<p data-start=3D"10202" data-end=3D"10264">how many miners per machine befo=
re latency starts to degrade</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10267" data-end=3D"10330">
<p data-start=3D"10269" data-end=3D"10330">keep your response-time distribu=
tion tight to maintain score.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"10332" data-end=3D"10335">
<h2 data-start=3D"10337" data-end=3D"10402">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What I=E2=
=80=99ll do next (without you needing to decide anything)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"10404" data-end=3D"10440">In the <em data-start=3D"10411" =
data-end=3D"10423">next steps</em>, I can start by:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"10442" data-end=3D"10686">
<li data-start=3D"10442" data-end=3D"10530">
<p data-start=3D"10445" data-end=3D"10530">Writing the <strong data-start=
=3D"10457" data-end=3D"10493">exact PyTorch <code data-start=3D"10473" data=
-end=3D"10485">TinyAgeNet</code> class</strong> (zk-friendly, with <code da=
ta-start=3D"10513" data-end=3D"10520">nonce</code> input).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10531" data-end=3D"10631">
<p data-start=3D"10534" data-end=3D"10631">Giving you a <strong data-start=
=3D"10547" data-end=3D"10575">template training script</strong> using the <=
code data-start=3D"10586" data-end=3D"10606">age_data/train.csv</code> + <c=
ode data-start=3D"10609" data-end=3D"10618">val.csv</code> structure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10632" data-end=3D"10686">
<p data-start=3D"10635" data-end=3D"10686">Then, an <strong data-start=3D"1=
0644" data-end=3D"10667">ONNX export snippet</strong> that=E2=80=99s ezkl-r=
eady.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"10688" data-end=3D"10796">You don=E2=80=99t have to send a=
nything for that =E2=80=94 I=E2=80=99ll just write it generically so you ca=
n drop it into your repo.</p>
<p data-start=3D"10798" data-end=3D"10985">If you <em data-start=3D"10805" =
data-end=3D"10809">do</em> want it tailored to your existing <code data-sta=
rt=3D"10844" data-end=3D"10867">train_tiny_age_net.py</code> or <code data-=
start=3D"10871" data-end=3D"10892">competition_circuit</code> layout, you c=
an paste those filenames / small snippets later and I=E2=80=99ll align exac=
tly to them.</p>
